{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Are there yet the treasures</b> — The honored man in the city, he yet holds to his wickedness after he heard the sound of the proclamation. In his house are treasures of wickedness. He gathered wealth through wickedness and with a diminished ephah, lacking, which is abhorrent to HaShem. And he does not say in his heart — he does not fear before HaShem — that he should say in his heart: I will profit with scales of wickedness."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The lemma renders only the opening words of the phrase; Ibn Ezra's comments appear to address the full verse. The Hebrew is compressed and paratactic; translated hyper-literally without connective tissue. The word עודהו ('he yet') is rendered as 'he yet holds.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:10.744769320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}